+> STOP. Captain's notes: non-binding. Captain writes, Captain trims. Anyone else: close this file now.
+
+# Captain Notes
+
+Binding behaviour lives in `features/**` specs and `assets/**`. History lives in git. These notes carry only what the next cycle needs.
+
+## Decisions captured
+- Framework label for the persistence key is `vanillajs`, so the localStorage name is `todos-vanillajs` (spec format `todos-[framework]`). Confirmed against the tastejs TodoMVC vanilla example convention.
+- Spec base markup is `assets/app-template.index.html`; CSS overrides live in `css/app.css`, base CSS untouched. App logic lives in `js/app.js` (vanilla, no preprocessors).
+- Persistence keys per item: `id`, `title`, `completed`. Editing mode is session-only and MUST NOT be persisted.
+- Routes required: `#/` (all, default), `#/active`, `#/completed`. Active filter persists across reload.
+
+## Open questions for the user
+- The package manifest (`package.json`) does not yet list `todomvc-common` or `todomvc-app-css`; the spec mandates them. Recorded under `## Dependencies` in `RIGGING.md` for Shipwright to install at fitting out. Does the user want the dependency install now, or defer to harbour?
+- Product dependencies `todomvc-common` / `todomvc-app-css` supply `base.css`, `index.css`, and `base.js`. The template references them under `node_modules/`. Confirm the relative paths stay as the template specifies.
+
+## Next role
+- QM, base commit `HEAD` (261606c). Scope is `watchbill.json` (watch1..watch6). Step definitions under `features/support/` and production code in `js/` and `index.html` are QM/Crew work, not Captain's.
