diff --git a/features/completing-todos.feature b/features/completing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..2267799
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/completing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+Feature: Completing todos
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to mark todos complete and clear finished work
+  So that I can track what remains
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Learn JS     | false     |
+      | Buy a unicorn | false     |
+
+  Rule: Completing a todo toggles its completed state and its styling
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a todo marks it completed
+    When the user toggles the todo "Learn JS"
+    Then the todo "Learn JS" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark-all checkbox completes every todo
+    When the user marks all todos as complete
+    Then every todo is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Mark-all checkbox reflects all-complete state
+    When the user toggles the todo "Learn JS"
+    And the user toggles the todo "Buy a unicorn"
+    Then the mark-all control is checked
+
+  Scenario: Clearing completed todos removes them and unchecks mark-all
+    Given the todo "Learn JS" is marked completed
+    When the user clears completed todos
+    Then the todo list has 1 item
+    And the mark-all control is unchecked
diff --git a/features/creating-todos.feature b/features/creating-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..0f2ae93
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/creating-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,33 @@
+Feature: Creating todos
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to add new todos through the top input
+  So that I can capture the work I need to do
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+
+  Rule: A non-empty trimmed title entered and confirmed creates exactly one todo
+
+  Scenario: New todo is appended when Enter is pressed
+    When the user types "Buy milk" into the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows "Buy milk"
+    And the todo list has 1 item
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is cleared after creation
+    When the user types "Walk the dog" into the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the new todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Whitespace-only new todo is ignored
+    When the user types "   " into the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+  Scenario: New todo is trimmed before creation
+    When the user types "  Water the plants  " into the new todo input
+    And the user presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows "Water the plants"
+
+  Scenario: New todo input is focused on page load
+    Then the new todo input is focused
diff --git a/features/editing-todos.feature b/features/editing-todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..017b852
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/editing-todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+Feature: Editing todos
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to rename a todo in place
+  So that I can correct a title without deleting the todo
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title    | completed |
+      | Taste JS | false     |
+
+  Rule: Editing commits a trimmed title, discards on escape, and deletes on empty
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a todo label enters edit mode
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Taste JS"
+    Then the todo "Taste JS" is in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo saves on Enter
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Taste JS"
+    And the user edits the title to "Taste JavaScript" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows "Taste JavaScript"
+    And the todo "Taste JavaScript" is not in edit mode
+
+  Scenario: Editing a todo saves on blur
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Taste JS"
+    And the user edits the title to "Taste ECMAScript" and blurs the field
+    Then the todo list shows "Taste ECMAScript"
+
+  Scenario: Empty edit removes the todo
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Taste JS"
+    And the user edits the title to "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list has 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards an in-progress edit
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Taste JS"
+    And the user edits the title to "Changed" and presses Escape
+    Then the todo list shows "Taste JS"
+    And the todo "Taste JS" is not in edit mode
diff --git a/features/list-summary.feature b/features/list-summary.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9879245
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/list-summary.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: List summary and visibility
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want the chrome to reflect my list state
+  So that I see only what is useful
+
+  Rule: Empty lists hide the main and footer; the count and clear button reflect state
+
+  Scenario: Empty list hides the main and footer sections
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer is hidden
+
+  Scenario: App is built on the template markup
+    Given the app is loaded with no todos
+    Then the page contains a new todo input
+    And the page contains a toggle-all control
+    And the page contains "All", "Active", and "Completed" filter links
+
+  Scenario Outline: Remaining count uses correct pluralization
+    Given the app has <count> active todos
+    Then the remaining count reads "<text>"
+
+    Examples:
+      | count | text         |
+      | 0     | 0 items left |
+      | 1     | 1 item left  |
+      | 2     | 2 items left |
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button hides when no completed todos
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | false     |
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button shows when completed todos exist
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | A     | true      |
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
diff --git a/features/persistence.feature b/features/persistence.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9ebc624
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/persistence.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+Feature: Persistence
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want my todos to survive a page reload
+  So that I do not lose my list
+
+  Rule: Todos are stored in localStorage under todos-vanillajs with id, title, and completed fields
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist across a page reload
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title   | completed |
+      | Ship it | false     |
+      | Fix bug | true      |
+    When the user reloads the app
+    Then the todo list shows "Ship it"
+    And the todo list shows "Fix bug"
+    And the todo "Fix bug" is marked completed
+
+  Scenario: Editing state is not persisted
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title   | completed |
+      | Edit me | false     |
+    When the user double-clicks the todo "Edit me"
+    And the user reloads the app
+    Then the todo "Edit me" is not in edit mode
+
+  @contract
+  Scenario: The localStorage todo record matches the required shape
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title | completed |
+      | Shape | true      |
+    Then the "todos-vanillajs" localStorage entry is a JSON array
+    And each stored todo has the fields "id", "title", and "completed"
diff --git a/features/routing.feature b/features/routing.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1c5480f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/routing.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+Feature: Routing and filters
+  As a user of the todo app
+  I want to filter the list by status
+  So that I can focus on active or completed work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded with todos:
+      | title   | completed |
+      | Active1 | false     |
+      | Done1   | true      |
+
+  Rule: Routes filter the visible list and mark the active filter link
+
+  Scenario: Active filter shows only incomplete todos
+    When the user opens the "Active" filter
+    Then the todo list shows "Active1"
+    And the todo list does not show "Done1"
+
+  Scenario: Completed filter shows only completed todos
+    When the user opens the "Completed" filter
+    Then the todo list shows "Done1"
+    And the todo list does not show "Active1"
+
+  Scenario: All filter shows every todo
+    When the user opens the "Completed" filter
+    And the user opens the "All" filter
+    Then the todo list shows "Active1"
+    And the todo list shows "Done1"
+
+  Scenario: Filter selection toggles the selected link
+    When the user opens the "Active" filter
+    Then the "Active" filter link is selected
+    And the "All" filter link is not selected
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across a reload
+    When the user opens the "Completed" filter
+    And the user reloads the app
+    Then the "Completed" filter link is selected
+    And the todo list shows "Done1"
